{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1360893-seeing-spirits-as-a-sin-eater","id":1360893,"title":"Seeing Spirits as a Sin-Eater","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-14T08:55:47-08:00","id":1360893,"title":"Seeing Spirits as a Sin-Eater","content":"In the Werewolf book Shunned By The Moon there is a mention of syncretic pack/krewes of Uratha and Bound, and I really love that idea. The main issue I have had with realizing this is a lack of common ground between the two. Werewolves have a Gift (Haunt equivalent) that allows them to see and interact with ghosts, so even though they don't normally have that capability, they can on an individual basis (such as a couple of PCs) have that ability. Sin-Eaters do not presently have a way to perceive or interact with Spirits that lack Death-related Influences or Numina. So, how could one give them that? Would it make sense for a Memento or a Ceremony to allow for it? A Regalia? Or should I just let Werewolves take care of Spirits and Sin-Eaters take care of Ghosts and have a more formal division of labor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T08:58:19-08:00","id":1360894,"title":"","content":"A totem could probably do it. And while not really something you would just get upon joining, if the Sin-Eaters were wolf-blooded they could have had a Tell that lets them see spirits (and everything else) in Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-14-2020, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T09:29:10-08:00","id":1360898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1360893-seeing-spirits-as-a-sin-eater?p=1360894#post1360894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A totem could probably do it. And while not really something you would just get upon joining, if the Sin-Eaters were wolf-blooded they could have had a Tell that lets them see spirits (and everything else) in Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't considered coming at it from the Werewolf side, but it makes sense to do it like that to increase the integration between the two. A totem doing it makes sense, and while I didn't realize that wolf-blooded keep their Tells if they gain a template, that would also make for a good crossover between the two. Thanks for the ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}